---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/')
  ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL
  : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;
---

<Layout title="About" description="About Naman, the things he keeps building, and what usually sends him down a new rabbit hole.">
  <div class="inner-page about-page">
    <section class="page-hero page-hero--split" aria-labelledby="about-title">
      <div>
        <p class="page-kicker">About / one curious person</p>
        <h1 id="about-title">I like turning small ideas into real things.</h1>
      </div>
      <div class="page-hero__aside about-intro">
        <img src={`${base}images/avatar.webp`} alt="Naman Patel" width="192" height="192" />
        <p>I’m Naman. Most of what I know came from building a version, breaking something, and staying curious long enough to understand it.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="about-layout">
      <div class="about-story">
        <section>
          <p class="section-number">01 / the pattern</p>
          <h2>Build first. Figure out the edges on the way.</h2>
          <p>That is how this site, Get Random Letter, and most of my experiments started. I find something interesting or annoying, build a version, test it, improve it, and write down what I learned.</p>
          <p>I like useful things, clear interfaces, weird little ideas, and the final ten percent that makes something feel finished instead of merely functional.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <p class="section-number">02 / what pulls me in</p>
          <h2>Search, products, tools, and the systems between them.</h2>
          <p>SEO is a big part of my work: technical fixes, content, search data, and figuring out why a useful page is not getting found. Building products pulled me deeper into web development, Android, automation, AI-assisted workflows, QA, and releases.</p>
          <p>I care less about which tool won the week than whether it helped make something genuinely useful.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <p class="section-number">03 / off screen</p>
          <h2>A little ambition, a little chaos, plenty of chai.</h2>
          <p><em>One Piece</em> is the permanent favorite. I like stories with ridiculous ambition, strange crews, and a world that keeps getting bigger the farther you go. Chai helps with the parts of building that somehow become 2 AM problems.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <p class="section-number">04 / why this site exists</p>
          <h2>I do not want everything I make to disappear into a feed.</h2>
          <p>I want one place where an Android utility can sit next to an open-source SEO tool, a weird browser experiment, an unfinished idea, and a post I still like six months later.</p>
          <p>Naman.blog is built with <a href="https://astro.build/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Astro</a>, mostly plain CSS, and a small amount of JavaScript. The setup stays intentionally boring so the things on the site can be less boring.</p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <aside class="now-card" aria-label="What Naman is doing now">
        <div><span>currently active</span><i></i></div>
        <dl>
          <dt>Making</dt><dd>Products, tools, and experiments</dd>
          <dt>Working on</dt><dd>SEO + search projects</dd>
          <dt>Writing</dt><dd>What I learn while doing it</dd>
          <dt>Recharging</dt><dd>One Piece + chai</dd>
        </dl>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
